DLG rocko
"""
{sequence
  - ROCKO: Gus. Dude. Our oral history report is due at 10 AM tomorrow.{pg}ROCKO: If we flunk, my mom sends me to live with Aunt Doris in Nebraska.{pg}ROCKO: And then the band, Velvet Thunderstorm, is OVER.
  - ROCKO: We still don't have a drummer, a bassist, or a single song. But the NAME, dude.
  - ROCKO: Go to the Quik-Stop and get us snacks. Snacks help us think.
  - ROCKO: {shk}Snacks, Gus.{/shk}
}
"""
NAME rocko

DLG guitar
You grab your air guitar. It is not plugged in. It never is. {wvy}Sick.{/wvy}
NAME guitar

DLG zip
"""
{sequence
  - {clr2}???{/clr2}: Greetings, Gus of the year 1988. I am ZIP-7, a courier from the year 2688.{pg}ZIP: In my time, the whole planet runs on the music of Velvet Thunderstorm.{pg}ZIP: But if you fail tomorrow's history report, the band breaks up and the future gets... {shk}super lame{/shk}.
  - ZIP: That arcade cabinet is the CHRONO-CADE. It can go anywhen.{pg}ZIP: Bring SIX great figures of history back to your school. Let THEM give your report.{pg}ZIP: Heads up: legends are busy people. Each one will want a favor first.{pg}ZIP: The bottom-right portal leads home. It will not open until six legends are aboard.
  - ZIP: Rocko will save your seats at the assembly. Now go! Time is, ironically, of the essence.
  - ZIP: {wvy}Bleep bloop. Rock on, past-human.{/wvy}
}
"""
NAME zip

DLG board
You drop a quarter into the CHRONO-CADE.{pg}{rbw}INSERT COIN... TIME TRAVEL!{/rbw}
NAME board

DLG to_athens
{clr2}ATHENS, GREECE - 399 BC{/clr2}
NAME to_athens

DLG to_france
{clr2}ORLEANS, FRANCE - 1429{/clr2}
NAME to_france

DLG to_vienna
{clr2}VIENNA, AUSTRIA - 1810{/clr2}
NAME to_vienna

DLG to_egypt
{clr2}ALEXANDRIA, EGYPT - 40 BC{/clr2}
NAME to_egypt

DLG to_dublin
{clr2}DUBLIN, IRELAND - 1921{/clr2}
NAME to_dublin

DLG to_mexico
{clr2}COYOACAN, MEXICO - 1940{/clr2}
NAME to_mexico

DLG to_future
{clr2}PINECREST, EARTH - 2688{/clr2}
NAME to_future

DLG to_hub
{wvy}whoosh{/wvy}
NAME to_hub

DLG to_home
"""
{
  - figs >= 6 ?
    {property locked false}ZIP (on the radio): Six legends aboard! Course set for Pinecrest High, 9:58 AM...{pg}ZIP: ...wait. Uh oh. Wrong coordinates. You're landing at Pinecrest MALL. At 9:30.{pg}ZIP: Do NOT let them wander off.
  - else ?
    {property locked true}ZIP (on the radio): Hold up, dude. You've only got {print figs} of 6 historical figures. Your report needs more history in it!
}
"""
NAME to_home

DLG student
"""
{sequence
  - YOUNG PLATO: You seek my teacher? He won't open his door until you answer his question.{pg}YOUNG PLATO: I wrote the answer on a scroll and hid it in the garden maze, south of here. For safekeeping. And drama.
  - YOUNG PLATO: I'm going to write ALL of this down someday.
}
"""
NAME student

DLG scroll
You found a scroll. It says one word, underlined three times: NOTHING.
NAME scroll

DLG gate_athens
"""
{
  - {item "l"} >= 1 ?
    {property locked false}SOCRATES (through the door): What is the only thing I truly know?{pg}GUS: (reading the scroll) Uh... NOTHING?{pg}SOCRATES: CORRECT. Come in, come in!
  - else ?
    {property locked true}SOCRATES (through the door): Before I go anywhere, answer me this: what is the only thing I truly know?{pg}GUS: Uh... how to make a sandwich?{pg}SOCRATES: Wrong! Come back when you know what I know.
}
"""
NAME gate_athens

DLG socrates
{figs = figs + 1}SOCRATES: You wish me to explain history to teenagers in the future?{pg}SOCRATES: I know only that I know nothing. So, honestly? I'll fit right in.{pg}{clr2}Socrates hops into the CHRONO-CADE. ({print figs}/6){/clr2}{exit "2" 2 4 "fade_w"}
NAME socrates

DLG guard
"""
{sequence
  - GUARD: The Maid sees no one without her banner. She dropped it somewhere in the woods to the west.{pg}GUARD: Again.
  - GUARD: The woods are a maze. Start from the south and keep left, I always say. I have never been in the woods.
}
"""
NAME guard

DLG banner
You found Joan's banner, slightly muddy. It still looks extremely inspiring.
NAME banner

DLG gate_france
"""
{
  - {item "n"} >= 1 ?
    {property locked false}GUARD: The banner! Pass, strange child with the strange hair.
  - else ?
    {property locked true}GUARD: Halt! None may enter without the Maid's banner.
}
"""
NAME gate_france

DLG goat
"""
{cycle
  - GOAT: Baa.
  - GOAT: Baaa. (It seems to believe in you.)
  - GOAT: {shk}BAAAA.{/shk}
}
"""
NAME goat

DLG joan
{figs = figs + 1}JOAN OF ARC: My banner! A voice told me a stranger would return it in a glowing box.{pg}GUS: That's... weirdly accurate.{pg}JOAN: I am not afraid. I was born to do this. Lead on.{pg}{clr2}Joan of Arc hops into the CHRONO-CADE. ({print figs}/6){/clr2}{exit "2" 6 4 "fade_w"}
NAME joan

DLG countess
"""
{sequence
  - COUNTESS: The maestro has lost three pages of his new piano piece. He is NOT taking it well.{pg}COUNTESS: One blew into the corner, one is in the closet, and one... who knows.
  - COUNTESS: Your trousers are extraordinary.
}
"""
NAME countess

DLG page
{pages = pages + 1}A page of sheet music! You have {print pages} of 3.
NAME page

DLG gate_vienna
"""
{
  - pages >= 3 ?
    {property locked false}You slide all three pages under the door. The shouting stops.{pg}The door creaks open.
  - else ?
    {property locked true}A sign on the door says MAESTRO AT WORK. From inside: muffled shouting about missing pages.{pg}(You have {print pages} of 3 pages.)
}
"""
NAME gate_vienna

DLG beethoven
{figs = figs + 1}BEETHOVEN: My pages! Thank you, strange boy.{pg}GUS: Wanna come to the future and be in our report?{pg}BEETHOVEN: {shk}WHAT?{/shk}{pg}GUS: (miming air guitar) RE-PORT. FU-TURE. ROCK.{pg}BEETHOVEN: Ah! Finally, someone who speaks music.{pg}{clr2}Beethoven hops into the CHRONO-CADE. ({print figs}/6){/clr2}{exit "2" 9 4 "fade_w"}
NAME beethoven

DLG fish
You found a fish by the river. It is a very good fish. Somebody would love this fish.
NAME fish

DLG cat
"""
{
  - catok == 1 ?
    TEMPLE CAT: (purrs smugly)
  - {item "f"} >= 1 ?
    {catok = 1}{item "f" 0}You offer the fish. The temple cat accepts it like it was always hers.{pg}{clr2}The temple cat approves of you.{/clr2}
  - else ?
    TEMPLE CAT: (stares at you like you owe it a fish)
}
"""
NAME cat

DLG gate_egypt
"""
{
  - catok == 1 ?
    {property locked false}The palace guards glance at the temple cat. The cat blinks. The guards step aside.
  - else ?
    {property locked true}PALACE GUARD: Nobody sees the Queen unless the temple cat approves.{pg}The temple cat looks unimpressed. And hungry.
}
"""
NAME gate_egypt

DLG cleopatra
{figs = figs + 1}CLEOPATRA: My cat approves of you. That has never happened. Explain yourself.{pg}GUS: Uh. Field trip? To 1988? There's a mall.{pg}CLEOPATRA: I speak nine languages. I will learn "mall."{pg}{clr2}Cleopatra hops into the CHRONO-CADE. ({print figs}/6){/clr2}{exit "2" 13 4 "fade_w"}
NAME cleopatra

DLG newsboy
"""
{pw = 1}{sequence
  - NEWSBOY: Extra, extra! Treaty talks in London!{pg}NEWSBOY: Looking for the Big Fellow, are ya? He sleeps somewhere different every night.{pg}NEWSBOY: Try the green door at the top of the street. Knock three times and say "the bicycle is outside."
  - NEWSBOY: Everyone knows he gets around Dublin on a bicycle. Nobody ever catches him on it, mind.
  - NEWSBOY: Three knocks. "The bicycle is outside." Off you go.
}
"""
NAME newsboy

DLG gate_dublin
"""
{
  - pw == 1 ?
    {property locked false}You knock three times. GUS: Um. The bicycle is outside?{pg}A long pause. The door opens a crack, then all the way.
  - else ?
    {property locked true}A voice behind the door: Wrong door, friend.{pg}(Maybe someone on the street knows how to get in.)
}
"""
NAME gate_dublin

DLG collins
{figs = figs + 1}MICHAEL COLLINS: You found me, which is more than the authorities ever managed.{pg}GUS: We need you for a history report. In 1988.{pg}COLLINS: History, is it? I've been rather busy making some. Go on, then. I'll come along.{pg}{clr2}Michael Collins hops into the CHRONO-CADE. ({print figs}/6){/clr2}{exit "2" 2 10 "fade_w"}
NAME collins

DLG gardener
"""
{sequence
  - GARDENER: Senora Frida won't open the studio. Her spider monkey, Fulang-Chang, ran off into the cactus garden.{pg}GARDENER: He likes the far east corner. Nobody can get in there. Except monkeys. And maybe you.
  - GARDENER: Mind the cactus. The cactus does not mind you.
}
"""
NAME gardener

DLG monkey
You scoop up Fulang-Chang the spider monkey. He immediately steals your sunglasses.
NAME monkey

DLG gate_mexico
"""
{
  - {item "k"} >= 1 ?
    {property locked false}Fulang-Chang squeaks at the door.{pg}FRIDA (inside): Fulang! You found him! Come in, come in!
  - else ?
    {property locked true}FRIDA (inside): Not now! My monkey has run off, and I cannot paint without him judging me.
}
"""
NAME gate_mexico

DLG frida
{figs = figs + 1}FRIDA KAHLO: You found my monkey. You may stay.{pg}GUS: Actually, we need YOU to come to 1988. For a school report.{pg}FRIDA: I paint myself because I am the subject I know best. Let's see what your century knows about itself.{pg}{clr2}Frida Kahlo hops into the CHRONO-CADE. ({print figs}/6){/clr2}{exit "2" 6 10 "fade_w"}
NAME frida

DLG futuredude
"""
{sequence
  - FUTURE DUDE: Whoa! Is that... GUS? From the Velvet Thunderstorm history scrolls?{pg}FUTURE DUDE: Everyone here learns your band's one rule in kindergarten:{pg}FUTURE DUDE: {rbw}Stay rad. Share your snacks.{/rbw}
  - FUTURE DUDE: We built a whole society on that. Works great, honestly.
  - FUTURE DUDE: Please don't flunk. My entire civilization is counting on you, no pressure.
}
"""
NAME futuredude

DLG cop
"""
{sequence
  - MALL COP: Hey! Are you responsible for the guy in the robe interrogating the corn dog stand?{pg}MALL COP: And the lady who drafted the sporting goods store into an army?{pg}MALL COP: Round them ALL up and get them out of my mall. Exit's on the east side.
  - MALL COP: All of them. Every last toga.
}
"""
NAME cop

DLG mall_socrates
{found = found + 1}SOCRATES is at the food court asking the corn dog guy what a corn dog truly IS. The corn dog guy is having a crisis.{pg}{clr2}Socrates rejoins the group. ({print found}/6){/clr2}
NAME mall_socrates

DLG mall_joan
{found = found + 1}JOAN OF ARC has bought every tennis racket in the sporting goods store and is training the shoppers into an army.{pg}{clr2}Joan of Arc rejoins the group. ({print found}/6){/clr2}
NAME mall_joan

DLG mall_beethoven
{found = found + 1}BEETHOVEN is playing the demo keyboard at Music Shack with the volume all the way up. He has invented synth-pop.{pg}{clr2}Beethoven rejoins the group. ({print found}/6){/clr2}
NAME mall_beethoven

DLG mall_cleopatra
{found = found + 1}CLEOPATRA is at the makeup counter, explaining eyeliner to the experts. They are taking notes.{pg}{clr2}Cleopatra rejoins the group. ({print found}/6){/clr2}
NAME mall_cleopatra

DLG mall_collins
{found = found + 1}MICHAEL COLLINS has the high score on every machine in the arcade, under the name BIG FELLOW.{pg}{clr2}Michael Collins rejoins the group. ({print found}/6){/clr2}
NAME mall_collins

DLG mall_frida
{found = found + 1}FRIDA KAHLO is in the photo booth, painting on the photo strip. It is now the most valuable photo strip on Earth.{pg}{clr2}Frida Kahlo rejoins the group. ({print found}/6){/clr2}
NAME mall_frida

DLG leave_mall
"""
{
  - found >= 6 ?
    {property locked false}MALL COP: ...and STAY out!{pg}You herd six legends across the parking lot to Pinecrest High. 9:59 AM.
  - else ?
    {property locked true}You can't leave yet. You've only rounded up {print found} of 6 legends. They're scattered around both halves of the mall.
}
"""
NAME leave_mall

DLG teacher
"""
{
  - found >= 6 ?
    MS. OKAFOR: Gus! You're late, and you've brought... guests? Well. Get up on that stage.
  - else ?
    MS. OKAFOR: Gus! You're late.
}
"""
NAME teacher

DLG rocko2
ROCKO: Dude! Where have you been?! And why is Beethoven eating a corn dog?{pg}ROCKO: Never mind. Get to the middle of the stage. We're on!
NAME rocko2

DLG fin
GUS & ROCKO present: "WHO WAS HISTORY?"{pg}SOCRATES tells the whole gym he knows nothing. The gym agrees with him. Huge applause.{pg}JOAN OF ARC gives a pep talk so fierce the football team wins three games that afternoon.{pg}BEETHOVEN plays the school piano so hard it falls off the stage. He cannot hear the cheering, but he can feel it.{pg}CLEOPATRA takes over student council by lunch.{pg}MICHAEL COLLINS explains how to negotiate a treaty. Three kids go on to become diplomats. Nobody can explain how he got to the gym.{pg}FRIDA KAHLO paints Ms. Okafor's portrait on the gym wall. Nobody is ever allowed to paint over it.{pg}MS. OKAFOR: ...A plus. A PLUS. I have no idea what just happened.{pg}Rocko stays in Pinecrest. Velvet Thunderstorm lives. The future is safe.{pg}{rbw}Stay rad. Share your snacks.{/rbw}{pg}THE END
